  "prefLabel": "Ed 1123.11 Local Education Agency Responsibilities when an Administrative Due Process Hearing Complaint is Filed",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1123.11 Local Education Agency Responsibilities when an Administrative Due Process Hearing Complaint is Filed. Each LEA shall:\n\n(a) Inform each parent that the parent has the right to request an administrative due process hearing to appeal the matters described in Ed 1123.03(a);\n\n(b) Provide each parent with the procedural safeguards notice as required by 34 CFR 300.504; and\n\n(c) Inform the parent or parents as required by 34 CFR 300.507(b) of any low-cost legal services and other relevant services available in the area.\n\nSource. (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ed 1100) #9197, eff 6-28-08; ss by #12141, eff 3-24-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html"
}
